Just ideas:
1. The Core Infrastructure (The "Nervous System")
A. Software & AI Stack
The Brain: Python (FastAPI) as the central logic hub.
The Vision: YOLOv8 (Label/QR Recognition) + Tesseract (OCR for Invoices).
The Comms: Twilio (SMS/Voice), WhatsApp Business API, and Gmail SMTP.
The Intelligence: OpenAI GPT-4o (Negotiation, Summarization, and Trend Analysis).
The Storage: Bi-directional Excel (Google Sheets API) for live inventory and financial logs.
B. Database Schema (Excel Sheets)
Master Wine DB: Metadata (Vintage, Varietal, Tasting Notes).
Live Inventory: Live Stock, In-Transit Qty, Thresholds, Validation Max (Fat-finger check), and "Last Alerted" level.
Provider Directory: Contact info, Primary vs. Alternative hierarchy, and Reliability Heatmap.
Financials: Burn rate, COGS, and Manual Purchase log.

2. Operational Workflows (Deep-Dive)
Workflow I: Inbound Logistics & Visual Tracking
Bottle Arrival: Camera identifies the label via YOLOv8.
State Check: System checks if an order was "In-Transit."
OCR Verification: Tesseract scans the physical invoice. It compares the Invoice Price vs. the AI-Negotiated Price.
The "Piece" Conversion: System prompts for "Cases Received." If 2 is entered, system calculates 2 * 12 = 24 bottles.
Manual Confirmation: Stock does not increase until the manager taps [Received]. This prevents "Ghost Inventory."
Workflow II: Real-Time Depletion & LIFO Notifications
Sale Trigger: POS records a sale (e.g., 4 bottles of Malbec).
Buffer Logic (30-min Window): buffer_manager.py collects all sales. It ignores intermediate stock drops (3, 2, 1).
LIFO Evaluation: At the 30-minute mark, it identifies the current state.
Notification Cascade: * If Stock goes <2,1,0, a Single Alert is sent via SMS/WhatsApp.
Shadow Stock Check: If Stock <0, trigger Inequality Alert (e.g., "Sold 2, but DB says 0. Did you buy more manually?").
One-Tap Correction: Manager taps [+2 Cases] on their phone to resolve the inequality instantly.
Workflow III: Autonomous Procurement & Negotiation
Threshold Hit: Stock <3 and no order is In-Transit.
Primary Contact: AI pings the Primary Provider via WhatsApp/Voice.
Alternative Cascade: If Primary is "Out of Stock" or price >10% higher than usual, AI pings the Alternative Provider.
The Summary: AI sends the manager a brief: "Provider X has 2 cases for $300. Accept?"
Vintage Substitution: If the year is different, AI adds a specific flag: "2019 is out; they offer 2020. OK?"
Workflow IV: Human-Automation Synchronization
Bi-Directional Watcher: If the manager opens/edits the Excel file, the sync_engine.py detects the lock.
"Yield to Human" Protocol: Automation pauses all writes for 30 seconds.
Conflict Notification: Manager gets a text: "Human edit detected; automation paused."
Fat-Finger Validation: If a manager enters a value >Validation_Max (e.g., 240 instead of 24 bottles), the system blocks the update and asks: "240 bottles added to Wine #2. Do you confirm?"

3. Reporting & Strategy (The "Executive Layer")
The Daily/Weekly Executive Digest (Gmail)
Live Stock Audit: List of all remaining bottles + "Critical" status items.
Financial Recap: Weekly spend vs. sales to ensure margin health.
Sales-to-Likeliness Ratio: A chart showing which wines are over-performing relative to their menu presence.
The "Loved Wine" Feedback: AI identifies the bottle with the highest velocity increase.
Reminder Digest: Any wine that is "Still Low" but hasn't been ordered is summarized here (to avoid SMS spam).

